        "original_id": "0f0730b0-d102-5ee2-b16b-963c3938866c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\"\n- People: Dallas Frazier\n- Organizations: The Oak Ridge Boys\n- Topics: album releases, singles, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- Fancy Free is the fifth country studio album by The Oak Ridge Boys, and it was released on March 26, 1981.\n- In 1981, Dallas Frazier's song \"Elvira\" became a famous country and pop hit for The Oak Ridge Boys and is considered one of their signature songs.\n- The songs \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles, but none of them charted within the top 40.",
